        {
          "en": "‘While it is good.’ He should lodge at an inn while the sun is still shining, and not wait until it becomes dark. In the morning he should not rise early to leave before it becomes light.\n\nContinuing the same comment, Rashi explains the phrase כי טוב: ‘For it is good.’ A favorable expression: ‘The light, that it was good.’ That is, it is good to go out and enter by it, because of harmful beings and robbers.",
          "explanation": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "en": "This is one continuous comment by Rashi. Its first part explains arriving at an inn before darkness and waiting for daylight before departure. Its continuation explains the wording “good” through “the light, that it was good”: light is the suitable time to enter and leave because of harmful beings and robbers. The later כי טוב continues that explanation rather than beginning a separate comment.",
                "he": "זהו דיבור אחד רצוף של רש״י: תחילתו מדריכה להגיע למלון בעוד אור ולצאת רק לאחר שהאיר היום, וסופו מסביר את לשון ״כי טוב״ באמצעות ״האור כי טוב״. האור הוא העיתוי הטוב לכניסה וליציאה בגלל המזיקים והלסטים. ״כי טוב״ בהמשך הוא חלק מאותו ביאור, ולא פתיחת דיבור נפרד."
              }
            ],
